@prefix rk:   <https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .

<https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk/mask-violation>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk> ;
    rdfs:label "Locus mask violation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """This file MUST make the ontology inconsistent.

K-A2 Term Incoherence requires a defined term whose satisfaction conditions can
empty out. Presenting facts are asserted, not defined, so the kernel marks the
crossing not well-formed and the module asserts it unsatisfiable.

Here a term incoherence is asserted to be part of a facts specification. If a
reasoner reports this consistent, the locus mask is documented but not
enforced.

This is a different failure from gating-violation.ttl and must be tested
separately: the mask can go inert while the gate still fires, and the reverse."""@en .

rk:factsSpec_1 a owl:NamedIndividual , rk:FactsSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "the presenting facts of some artifact"@en .

rk:incoherence_1 a owl:NamedIndividual , rk:KA2 ;
    rdfs:label "a term incoherence asserted at presenting facts"@en ;
    obo:BFO_0000050 rk:factsSpec_1 .
